<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1232" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aenĕădēs</span></b> ,
		ae (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>gen. plur.</i> Aeneadūm, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 1,
			1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. Tr. 2, 261</span></i>), <i>patr.
				m.</i> [Aeneas]. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A descendant of Æneas; his son
			Ascanius</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 9, 653</span></i> (<i>Aenides</i>, Rib.).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In gen., <i>those who are related in
				any manner to Æneas;</i> nence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A Trojan</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 7,
				616</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 565</span></i>; but oftener, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A Roman</i>, Verg. a. 8, 648; <i><span class="en">Ov.
				M. 15, 682, 695 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>An adulatory epithet of Augustus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. P. 1,
				1, 35</span></i>; <i>of Scipio</i>, <i><span class="en">Sil. 13,
				767</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
